Googology/Notation/Y/WellOrder/ZeroY/, Googology/Notation/Y/WellOrder/OneY/ and
Googology/Notation/Y/WellOrder/Por/

  These files are taken from koteitan, 1y-wo-por
  https://github.com/koteitan/1y-wo-por
  revision db86f2d13c2e18a8e2c2fae5e083d00fc4d48a78 (Apache-2.0),
  and ported from Lean 4.33.1 / Mathlib v4.33.1 to Lean 4.30.0 /
  Mathlib v4.30.0. The port renames the module names in the imports (prefix
  `Googology.Notation.Y.WellOrder.`) and changes a few proofs; each file's
  header says what was changed.

  1y-wo-por in turn contains code adapted from

    Phyrion, 1Y-Well-Ordering-Lean
    https://github.com/Phyrion1343/1Y-Well-Ordering-Lean
    revision 6533b2975f3cafb3582dc8f8127e9ea7144d7e69 (Apache-2.0)

  (ZeroY/ and OneY/, adapted from `formalization/ZeroY` and
  `formalization/OneY`), and helpers of koteitan, bms-elem-pattern
  (https://github.com/koteitan/bms-elem-pattern), released under Apache-2.0
  by the same author (Por/Tuple.lean, Por/Omega1.lean, Por/Relation.lean,
  Por/Closure.lean, Por/Chain.lean). Each file keeps the header that names its
  origin. Por/BMS/ was written for 1y-wo-por. No code from the unlicensed
  snapshot that 1Y-Well-Ordering-Lean vendors as `vendor/bms` is copied or
  adapted.

Googology/Notation/OmegaY/WellOrder/, Googology/Notation/OmegaY/Official.lean
and test/OmegaYCheck.lean

  These files are taken from koteitan, wy-wo-por
  https://github.com/koteitan/wy-wo-por
  revision 7038635644b8d1df3f0f1a80f107210da7e33a94 (Apache-2.0),
  and ported from Lean 4.33.1 / Mathlib v4.33.1 to Lean 4.30.0 /
  Mathlib v4.30.0. The port renames the module names in the imports (prefix
  `Googology.Notation.OmegaY.WellOrder.`), imports the 0-Y modules and the BMS
  layer from Googology/Notation/Y/WellOrder/ZeroY/ and
  Googology/Notation/Y/WellOrder/Por/ instead of copying them (wy-wo-por
  takes the same files from koteitan/1y-wo-por, revision
  db86f2d13c2e18a8e2c2fae5e083d00fc4d48a78), renames the namespace `Por` of
  Por/Formula.lean, Por/Relation.lean and Por/Supply.lean to `OmegaY.Por`,
  sets `backward.do.legacy false` in every file, and changes a few proofs;
  each file's header says what was changed. OmegaY/Official/Build.lean of
  wy-wo-por, the official expansion, is moved to
  Googology/Notation/OmegaY/Official.lean. test/OmegaYCheck.lean is
  OmegaY/Official/Check.lean of wy-wo-por, without its closing `#eval`.

  wy-wo-por in turn contains code adapted from

    Phyrion, omega-Y-Well-Ordering-Lean
    https://github.com/Phyrion1343/omega-Y-Well-Ordering-Lean
    revision 33c16a8ce8f7e01bb3794881f3ff9109474beaed (Apache-2.0)

  (the modules under OmegaY/ other than OmegaY/Official/). Each of these files
  keeps the header that names its original path and says what was changed:
  `YesMetaZFC.BMS.transGen_head` is replaced by `Por.BMS.transGen_head` (same
  statement; of the files that used it, only OmegaY/Forests.lean is ported
  here), and the reflection layer
  (OmegaY/Reflection.lean, OmegaY/Reflection/Interface.lean,
  OmegaY/Reflection/OrdinalSupply.lean, OmegaY/KeyReflection.lean) is proved
  from the patterns-of-resemblance model in Por/ instead of Phyrion's
  recursion. Por/Supply.lean adapts `Label`, `top`, `countable_iio_ordinal`
  and `countable_iio` of OmegaY/Reflection/OrdinalSupply.lean of that project
  and says so in its header. OmegaY/Official/ (the official omega-Y expansion,
  a modification of Phyrion's weak-magma expansion, and the proof that it is
  well founded) and Por/Formula.lean, Por/Relation.lean and Por/Supply.lean
  were written for wy-wo-por by the same author as this repository. No code
  from the unlicensed snapshot of YesMetaZFC / BMS-Well-Ordering-Lean that
  omega-Y-Well-Ordering-Lean depends on is copied or adapted.

  The official omega-Y expansion is defined by `expand` of Naruyoko,
  StudyAndExpandSequence (https://github.com/Naruyoko/StudyAndExpandSequence,
  revision b26ba7e5fc2c8edb4065f1d721855a7e0e644ff2), which has no license.
  None of its code is used: Googology/Notation/OmegaY/Official.lean is written
  from a description of the rule, and the program was only run to record the
  expected values in test/OmegaYCheck.lean.

